From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:30:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Outfits: fabrics from a description, a seamless swatch as
 a fill

characters/outfit/fabric.py is stage 2 of the outfits
(docs/research/outfit_textures.md): a description such as "blue paisley
silk" becomes seamless fabric swatches from a text-to-image model, and
the chosen one tiles over a garment like any Swatch, keeping the
garment's folds and stitching.

- The description is tidied and checked against small, extensible kiosk
  word lists (fabric_words.json: brands, characters, logos, offensive
  words, matched whatever their case, accents, spacing or look-alike
  digits); it goes into the review's template.
- A keyword preview comes first, then the fallback ladder: FLUX.2 [klein]
  4B at 4 steps, at 12 steps, SD-Turbo, the model-free repair of the best
  image, the keyword fabric, a plain colour. Each step down says why.
  Missing packages, weights or network go straight to the keyword fabric
  with the install or download command; a model that fails (out of
  memory, an error) is not tried again at more steps.
- tiling.py makes a model paint a repeat for one call: the transformer
  pipelines' latents are rolled in callback_on_step_end (FLUX.2's packed
  tokens unpacked to their grid, Z-Image's grid by whole 2 x 2 patches;
  random offsets shrinking to none for the last step, the total undone),
  their VAE decoder pads circularly, and SD-Turbo's UNet and VAE pad
  circularly. Both are undone afterwards, also after errors and cancels,
  under the pipeline's lock.
- seamless.py: a seam score (a step, a line or a broken rhythm at the
  wrap against the inside of the image, in Lab) ranks seeds and leaves
  out those above 1.25; a deterministic repair for any image (rolled by
  half, the cross quilted along a minimum-error cut with the coarse
  colour cross-faded, a wider fade for smooth fabric); even light (the
  light that varies once across the swatch divided out, colours kept).
- FabricJob: a daemon worker thread, results as they come (poll or
  iterate, callbacks), the keyword preview first, cancelling at the next
  denoising step, progress, a pace hook.
- A cache of finished swatches in the git-ignored fabrics/, by prompt,
  model, seed, size and method; a description that is all cached never
  loads the model.
- The Fabric fill (fabric_fill, FabricSwatch.fill): its spec records the
  description, prompt, model, seed, method and the image (a lossless WebP
  data URI), so Outfit specs and saved created characters rebuild it
  without the model; a scale per kind of fabric, which can be set.

people/generator.py: ImageGenerator.rgb() takes a step count and pipeline
arguments; a lock per pipeline; local_files_only; shared_generator()
loads each model once per process. fills.py: lossless WebP data URIs,
swatches resampled as repeats for the mipmaps (a 768 px swatch kept a
seam line there), {"fabric": ...} specs.

CLI: bifold-characters fabric "..." -o swatch.png [--model ...] [--seeds 4]
[--size 512] [--sheet all.png] [--avatar NAME --region top --views
views.png] [--offline].

Tests (tests/test_fabric.py): stand-in pipelines with the latent layouts
of Flux2KleinPipeline, ZImagePipeline and an SD UNet pipeline; tiny
randomly initialised diffusers models built in the test, no downloads (a
VAE decoder that tiles once it pads circularly, a UNet, a
Flux2KleinPipeline whose rolled run equals the plain one with its
transformer zeroed, Z-Image and SD pipelines); the seam score, the repair
and the light on synthetic textures; the ladder rung by rung; the filter,
the cache, cancelling, results as they come; spec round trips through
Outfit and created characters; the CLI; a real avatar rendered in a
fabric. A README section with notes for the Mac, and
docs/previews/fabric.jpg (synthetic and procedural textures only: no
model ran here).

